# Module Boundary Rules

Policy: [docs/architecture/core-platform-convention.md](docs/architecture/core-platform-convention.md), [docs/architecture/contributing-modules.md](docs/architecture/contributing-modules.md), [docs/architecture/erp-shared-master.md](docs/architecture/erp-shared-master.md)

- Reuse Shared Master (`Supplier`, `Branch`, `Unit`) — do not add per-module Vendor/Customer/Branch tables. See [erp-shared-master.mdc](erp-shared-master.mdc).
- `app/api/**` is a thin adapter only: auth, parse request, call `modules/*/application`, map response — no heavy business logic or ad-hoc Prisma in the route.
- Do not import `@/lib/prisma` from `app/api/**/route.ts` — use application services or `@/shared/db` where allowed. Exceptions only per convention §4 (e.g. NextAuth adapter, reviewed cron).
- Do not query another module's domain tables from `modules/A` — call that module's application service instead.
- Application services throw `AppError` subclasses (`ForbiddenError`, `NotFoundError`, `ValidationError`, `UnauthorizedError`); `withAuth` / route handlers map them to JSON.
- New domain logic belongs under `modules/<name>/application` (and `domain` / `infra` when needed), not under `app/`.

# Verification

- Import direction matches the core-platform diagram (`app` → application/shared; application → own domain/infra + shared).
- ESLint `no-restricted-imports` for `@/lib/prisma` remains satisfied where configured.
- Changed routes stay thin; business rules live in application services.
